       src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#@@ -0,0 +1,771 @@
  3. [in_service] `measure_instability` defaults to applying `DEFAULT_PERTURBATION`, so a plain harness run will always create and measure a perturbation unless the caller explicitly disables it. The obligations require a default perturbation parameter, but not that perturbation be enabled by default.
       src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#@@ -0,0 +1,771 @@
  4. [in_service] The harness introduces a new `Mode.RECORD` requirement for measurement runs and explicitly rejects replay as the measurement mode. The obligations require independent draws and recording provenance, but they do not require changing the measurement mode semantics or asserting that replay is never used.
