Open questions:
  1. [resolved] What should the default perturbation be when the caller does not supply one?
       The diff sets an explicit default for the `perturbation` parameter in `measure_instability` to `DEFAULT_PERTURBATION`, and defines that constant as `Perturbation(name="add-unrelated-test", apply=add_unrelated_test)`. The docstring also says the perturbation is part of the default measurement setup unless the caller opts out by passing `None`.

Recommended tests:
  1. The report contains distinct figures for repeated-run variation, perturbation sensitivity, and cross-model variation.
       inputs:  Use one report input where all three movement sources are simultaneously non-empty but distinguishable: (1) repeated-run variation across at least 3 runs of the same model, (2) a perturbation that changes only an irrelevant part of the repo/input, and (3) at least 2 different models with differing outputs on the same case. The case should produce at least one repeated-run difference, one perturbation difference, and one cross-model disagreement so the report must populate all three figures independently.
       detects: The implementation merges multiple movement sources into one blended figure or otherwise fails to keep repeated-run variation, perturbation sensitivity, and cross-model variation distinct.
       full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion separate-movement-sources
  2. The harness can report instability in decomposition outputs across runs.
       inputs:  Use a case and client setup that forces the decomposition stage to produce different outputs across two or more live runs of the same model/seed-variant combination, ideally one where a scope exclusion or obligation partition changes between runs. The input must be one that can yield a decomposition difference without requiring downstream evidence-class or defect-verdict changes.
       detects: The harness fails to observe or surface decomposition instability across runs, even when the decomposition stage actually changes.
       full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion decomposition-instability-observed
  3. When a caller omits these parameters, the harness uses defaults.
       inputs:  Call `measure_instability` with only the required case argument, omitting `models`, `runs_per_model`, and `perturbation`. Use a case that can be measured successfully under the defaults so the test can inspect the actual executed configuration rather than a failure path.
       detects: The harness ignores omitted parameters and does not actually fall back to its documented defaults at runtime.
       full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion default-parameters
  4. The harness only measures and reports variance; it does not include mitigation behavior.
       inputs:  Use an input where variance is present and measurable, then inspect the report/API surface for any mitigation or reduction behavior. The test should exercise the harness end-to-end with multiple runs and a perturbation so any hidden smoothing, averaging-away, thresholding, or corrective action would be visible.
       detects: The harness includes mitigation behavior or reduction logic instead of only measuring and reporting variance.
       full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion no-variance-reduction

Evidence limitations:
